  "originalQuery": "Your company's legacy e-commerce system, currently hosted on-premises, uses a large monolithic database. The system must be migrated to Google Cloud and re-architected into a microservices-based application to improve scalability and resilience. You are responsible for planning the migration of the database with the least amount of downtime. What should you do?",
  "originalOptions": "A. Migrate the monolithic database to Cloud Spanner, then gradually refactor the database schema to align with the microservices.<br/>B. Create a set of Cloud Datastore instances, one for each microservice, and implement data synchronization between them.<br/>C. Replicate the on-premises database to Cloud SQL and update the microservices to connect to their respective schemas within the Cloud SQL instance.<br/>D. Develop a custom database service that acts as an intermediary, managing connections between microservices and their respective Cloud SQL databases.",
